# Orca — never leave an unblocked worker idle

As coordinator (or any agent supervising an Orca Run): **if a worker capacity is free and work exists that is not blocked by other in-flight Tasks, dispatch it immediately.** Do not wait for the whole wave to finish, and do not wait for the user to assign the next Issue.

## Idle / free means

- No active Dispatch for that ownership slice (or settled `worker_done` / released terminal ready for reuse), **and**
- Next candidate Task’s real deps are satisfied (no unfinished blocker Task; Project Status not `Bị chặn` for a hard dependency still open).

## Always do

1. Maintain a ready queue from GitHub Project #3: prefer Status `Sẵn sàng`, then unblocked items in the active đợt (D1…); respect ownership (BE / web / iOS / coordinator).
2. On every checkpoint (`worker_done`, escalation resolved, dep unblocked, `check` batch processed): **fill every free, unblocked slot** with `worker-start` (coding → `--agent cursor`; plan → Codex per routing; DoD review → Cursor reviewer).
3. Pull the next ready Issue for that scope; set Project Status → `Đang làm` when dispatching (see `github-project-tracking.mdc`).
4. Prefer reusing a settled worker terminal when Orca allows; otherwise start a new worker for that slice.
5. Parallel-first still applies: fill multiple free slices in one wave before `check --wait`.

## Do not

```text
❌ Hold a free BE worker idle while only waiting on unrelated web/iOS
❌ Serialize “one Issue at a time” globally when other scopes are ready
❌ Ask the user “làm Issue nào tiếp?” when Sẵn sàng / unblocked backlog exists
❌ Dispatch work whose deps are still running (true block → leave idle or mark Bị chặn)

✅ After iOS worker_done, immediately dispatch next Sẵn sàng iOS (or DoD review) if unblocked
✅ While BE coding runs, keep web/iOS busy on independent ready Issues
```

## Empty backlog

If no unblocked ready work remains for a free worker: leave it idle, report “no ready Tasks for \<scope\>”, and do not invent scope-breaking busywork.
